course: dictionary
lesson: 3840
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word fortune can mean a very large amount of money, luck, or what will happen to you in the future. «That car cost a fortune» is about money, so the clue is cost.
explain: «By good fortune, the rain stopped just before the match.» Good fortune means good luck. The rain stopping at the right moment was lucky, not planned. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases have their own meaning. «Make a fortune» means earn a lot of money, and «tell someone's fortune» means say what will happen to them in the future. A fortune teller says she can see the future, but in real life nobody can, so her claims are not facts.
fact: Fortune is a noun with three main meanings: a lot of money, luck, and what will happen to a person in the future.
fact: «Good fortune» means good luck, and «by good fortune» means by luck.
fact: «Seek their fortune» in a story means go out into the world to become rich and happy.
fact: «Lady Luck» means chance or fortune, spoken of as if she were a person.
fact: Nobody can really see the future, so a fortune teller's claims are not facts.
exercise: «That car cost a fortune.» What does a fortune mean here? | *A very large amount of money | A map of the roads | A small amount of change | Luck on a long journey
exercise: «They won the prize by good fortune, not by skill.» What does good fortune mean? | *Good luck | A happy memory | A large bill | Hard work
exercise: What does «tell someone's fortune» mean? | Ask them their name | Give them a prize | *Say what will happen to them in the future | Tell them a joke
test: «He made a fortune selling his old bikes.» What does made a fortune mean? | Bought a map of the city | Lost all his money | Built a bike from scratch | *Earned a very large amount of money
test: In a story, a hero sets off to seek their fortune. What does that mean? | To look for a lost coin in the garden | *To go out into the world to become rich and happy | To stay at home and sleep | To ask the king for a horse
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The fortune teller said the new school would be awful»? | Good luck on a test | *What will happen to you in the future | A small shop on the corner | A very large amount of money
